# TypeScript coding rules

Detail: [docs/knowledge/typescript/README.md](../docs/knowledge/typescript/README.md)

## Types

- ❌ `any` (including test code unless unavoidable with narrow escape hatch)
- ✅ `unknown` + type guards / Zod `.parse()` / `.safeParse()`
- ✅ Generics for reusable hooks, services, and API responses

## Constants vs enum

- ❌ TypeScript `enum` for string unions
- ✅ `as const` object + derived union type:

```typescript
export const ROLE = {
  ADMIN: 'admin',
  USER: 'user',
} as const;

export type Role = (typeof ROLE)[keyof typeof ROLE];
```

- ✅ Zod `z.enum([...])` for runtime validation (not TS `enum`)

## Feature types

- Domain types in `features/<name>/types/`
- Shared API shapes from `@repo/api` when contract is cross-stack
- Export public types via `features/<name>/index.ts` only when needed outside the feature
